Subject: [PATCH 10/14] libcamera: pipeline: ipu3: Power the lens only while
 the camera runs

Open the lens subdev when the camera starts and close it when the camera
stops, so that the lens, and through the runtime PM device link the
camera sensor, can be powered down while the camera is idle.

On the Microsoft Surface Pro 5 the rear ov8865 sensor with its dw9719
lens otherwise stays powered permanently as soon as WirePlumber is
running. With this change both are runtime suspended while the camera
is idle, are resumed when it starts, autofocus moves the lens as before,
and both are suspended again about one second after the camera stops.

Signed-off-by: Marco Ziliani <rylos78@gmail.com>
